524
00:34:04.262 --> 00:34:12.283
Sampling: keeping 1% of INFO traces cut stored volume to 3% while keeping every ERROR (and every error trace whole).

525
00:34:12.563 --> 00:34:16.105
Sample by trace, never by line, and never sample errors.

526
00:34:16.385 --> 00:34:26.774
Cardinality: a counter labelled by (service, level, userid) would create ~18,530 time series; by (service, level) only 10.

527
00:34:27.054 --> 00:34:32.174
High-cardinality identifiers belong in logs and traces, not metric labels.

